// Both arms of the branch write z := 1, so z := 1 should not depend on rc.
// Each z := 1 has two unordered immediate ppo-predecessors: the initial write
// of z (same location) and the acquire read of y (an acquire read precedes
// everything after it). Lifting compares the two writes and their
// predecessors. Compared pair by pair, it would need the initial write of z to
// be equivalent to the read of y, the lift would fail, and the control
// dependency rc -> z := 1 would close the load-buffering cycle through
// thread 2. MoRDor matches predecessors back and forth: each one on one side
// with an equivalent one on the other. The writes lift, as the program with
// the branch removed (acq-other-loc-nobranch.lit) is allowed.
x := 0; y := 0; z := 0; c := 0;
{
  r2 :acq= y;
  rc := c;
  if (rc = 1) {
    z := 1;
  } else {
    z := 1;
  };
} ||| {
  r3 := z;
  c := r3
}
%%
allow (rc = 1 && r3 = 1) [smrd]
